## Probability and Expected Values

You have a four sided die, which has the numbers 1, 3, 5 and 7 on each side. The die is fair so each of
these values is equally likely.

Q1:   Let X represent the sum of two independent rolls of the die.  What is E[X]? Write down the formula and give an estimate.
[ for 1 roll 1*.25 + 3*.25 + 5 * .25 + 7 * .25 = 16*.25 = 4; for 2 it is then 8.]

Q2: if you roll the die twice and get a sum of 12, what is the chance that your friend rolls the die twice and gets a higher score?

Q3:  Write code to estimate the mean and variance of the sum of 10 rolls of the die.


## Regression and Modeling

```{r, echo=FALSE}
dat1 = read.csv("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencelabs/2024/refs/heads/main/data/midterm-2/trial.csv")

m1 = lm(outcome~treatment, data=dat1)

m2 = lm(outcome ~ treatment + group, data=dat1)

m3 = lm(outcome ~ treatment * group, data=dat1)

```

